          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: In July 2008, a witness reported an observation made at night in 1980 or 1981 with two other family members along the N-S axis of the Lyon-Avignon highway. For approximately thirty seconds, they observed a glowing ball that then split into three stationary entities before disappearing into the sky at very high speed. Our requests for additional information (particularly regarding the date, which is given arbitrarily here) have gone unanswered to date, and we lack information and details about this observation.",
